    "digdeeper": {
      "type": "zeta-accordion",
      "blocks": {
        "a1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Description",
            "content": "<p>The ZETA MEGAS formula features <strong>MaxSimil® monoglyceride fish oil</strong>, which delivers a <strong>three times greater EPA + DHA absorption rate</strong> than equivalent doses of standard fish oils. Through MaxSimil's patented PLATform (Pre-digested Lipid Absorption Technology), omega-3s are delivered in their pre-processed monoglyceride form — bypassing the digestion step that limits absorption of triglyceride and ethyl ester fish oils.</p><p>Each daily serving delivers 1,300 mg of high-purity omega-3s with the EPA + DHA ratio your body uses for inflammation management, brain health, cardiovascular support, and skin.*</p><ul>\n<li>Supports cardiovascular health — triglycerides, blood pressure, vessel function</li>\n<li>Supports brain function — cognition, mood, memory</li>\n<li>Supports healthy inflammatory response</li>\n<li>Supports joint comfort and mobility</li>\n<li>Supports skin elasticity and barrier function</li>\n<li>Supports eye health (DHA is concentrated in the retina)</li>\n</ul><p style=\"font-size:11px;color:var(--zeta-mid);font-style:italic;margin-top:20px;\">*These statements have not been evaluated by the Food and Drug Administration. This product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease.</p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "a2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Ingredients",
            "content": "<p><strong>MaxSimil® Monoglyceride Fish Oil — 1,300 mg per serving (2 softgels).</strong></p><ul>\n<li>EPA (Eicosapentaenoic acid) — ~715 mg</li>\n<li>DHA (Docosahexaenoic acid) — ~410 mg</li>\n<li>Other omega-3 fatty acids — remainder</li>\n</ul><p><strong>Other Ingredients:</strong> Bovine gelatin (softgel), glycerin, water, natural lemon flavor, mixed tocopherols (antioxidant).</p><p><strong>Sourcing + Purity:</strong> Sustainably sourced from small wild-caught cold-water fish (anchovy, sardine, mackerel). Third-party tested for heavy metals, PCBs, and oxidation. Below all international standards for omega-3 purity.</p><p><strong>Why this form:</strong> Triglyceride and ethyl ester fish oils need lipase enzymes to break them down before absorption. MaxSimil delivers omega-3s in monoglyceride form — the form your gut would produce mid-digestion anyway — skipping the bottleneck. Up to 3× more EPA and DHA make it into your bloodstream.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "a3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Directions & Precautions",
            "content": "<p><strong>Take 2 softgels daily.</strong> Most people take both in the morning. Unlike standard fish oils, MaxSimil absorbs well with or without food — you can take it on an empty stomach if that fits your routine.</p><p><strong>Pairs well with:</strong> ZETA D+K (both fat-soluble; they support each other's absorption), ZETA MULTI (the daily foundation), ZETA LONGEVITY (for the long-game antioxidant stack).</p><p><strong>Precautions:</strong> If you're on blood thinners (warfarin, aspirin, Plavix), check with your physician — omega-3s at high doses can affect clotting. If pregnant, nursing, or have a fish/shellfish allergy, consult your healthcare provider. Don't exceed 2 softgels per day.</p><p style=\"font-size:11px;color:var(--zeta-mid);font-style:italic;\">*These statements have not been evaluated by the Food and Drug Administration. This product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "a4": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Research",
            "content": "<div class=\"acc-highlight\">\n<div class=\"hl-label\">★ Key publication · MaxSimil absorption</div>\n<p><strong>Cuenoud B et al. (2020)</strong> — Monoglyceride form of omega-3 fatty acids increases EPA+DHA absorption: a randomized crossover study. <em>Clinical Nutrition.</em> The study demonstrating MaxSimil's 3× EPA+DHA absorption advantage over standard fish oil forms.</p>\n</div><div class=\"ref\">\n<strong>Calder PC. (2017)</strong> — Omega-3 fatty acids and inflammatory processes: from molecules to man. <em>Biochemical Society Transactions.</em> Comprehensive review of EPA and DHA's role in resolving inflammation at the cellular level.</div><div class=\"ref\">\n<strong>Mozaffarian D, Wu JHY. (2011)</strong> — Omega-3 fatty acids and cardiovascular disease: effects on risk factors, molecular pathways, and clinical events. <em>Journal of the American College of Cardiology.</em>\n</div><div class=\"ref\">\n<strong>Dyall SC. (2015)</strong> — Long-chain omega-3 fatty acids and the brain: a review of the independent and shared effects of EPA, DPA and DHA. <em>Frontiers in Aging Neuroscience.</em>\n</div>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        }
      },
